  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-218538",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To multiply a complex number by a purely imaginary number, we use the distributive property and the fact that ${i}^{2}=-1.$\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4\\,\\text{i})\\cdot (2+3\\,\\text{i}) & =(-4\\,\\text{i})\\cdot 2+(-4\\,\\text{i})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot 2\\,\\text{i}+(-4)\\cdot 3\\cdot {\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & =-8\\,\\text{i}+(-12)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-8\\,\\text{i}+12 \\\\  & =12-8\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
